{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790514400437,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e2f8bbaf001qzXIv2GkHaiEis","messageID":"msg_0e2f8b154001Lhsyj51DRetBwh","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I need to understand the score situation. The bot currently scores 0.091. Let me look at the key issues. From the code and the comments, I can see several important things:\n\n1. The `anger_peaceful_dwarf` strategy in `global_logic.py` - this is about angering peaceful dwarves in the Mines to get a pick-axe. This is important for non-gnome/dwarf roles.\n\n2. The `global_strategy` method chains together various strategies with preemption.\n\n3. The `current_strategy` method handles the milestone-based progression.\n\n4. The `fight2` strategy in `agent.py` handles combat.\n\n5. The `elbereth_action` in `fight_heur.py` - engraving Elbereth is important for survival.\n\n6. The `dip_for_excalibur` strategy - getting Excalibur is important for lawful characters.\n\nLet me think about what might be causing the low score of 0.091. The score is BALROG progression. Looking at the code comments and the structure:\n\n- The bot goes through Dlvl 1 grind, then Mines, then main dungeon\n- The key to good scores is getting deep (descending) and surviving\n- The `anger_peaceful_dwarf` strategy is specifically for getting a pick-axe from a peaceful dwarf\n\nLet me look at what identities this bot plays. The identity is `hea-gno-neu-mal` based on the task description. That's Healer-Gnome-Neutral-Male.\n\nLet me check the character configuration more carefully. The identity `hea-gno-neu-mal` means:\n- role: HEALER (3)\n- race: GNOME (3) \n- alignment: NEUTRAL (1)\n- gender: MALE (0)\n\nSo this bot plays a Healer-Gnome-Neutral-Male.\n\nNow, let me think about what's going wrong for a Healer-Gnome. From the code:\n\n1. Healers are in `ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY` - so they should leave the Dlvl 1 grind when hungry\n2. Gnomes are in `MINES_FOLK_ROUTE` - so they walk peaceful Mines to Mines' End\n3. But Healer is not a typical \"mines folk\" role\n\nLooking at the global_logic more carefully:\n\n- `MINES_FOLK_ROUTE = True` - gnomes and dwarves walk peaceful Mines\n- `ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY` includes `Character.MONK` and `Character.WIZARD` but NOT Healer\n- Healer is not in `ROLES_WITHOUT_MINES_ROUTES` so it does have mines routes\n\nWait, let me re-read the `current_strategy` method more carefully. The milestone-based progression is key.\n\nFor a Healer-Gnome-Neutral-Male:\n1. Starts at BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL milestone\n2. The condition checks `experience_level >= _grind_xl()` or `LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and hunger_state >= HUNGRY and total_nutrition == 0`\n3. `_grind_xl()` returns `ROLE_GRIND_XL.get(character.role, GRIND_XL)` which defaults to 8 for Healer\n4. So Healer should leave the grind at XP 8\n\nBut wait - the Healer role has some specific considerations. Let me look at the ` ROLE_GRIND_XL` and `ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY`:\n- `ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY` includes `Character.WIZARD` but NOT `Character.HEALER`\n- So Healer will NOT leave the grind when hungry - it will keep grinding on Dlvl 1\n\nThis could be a major issue. Healers need to leave the Dlvl 1 grind to get down to deeper levels where they can score better. If they stay grinding on Dlvl 1 forever, they'll never descend.\n\nActually, wait. Looking more carefully at the condition in `current_strategy`:\n\n```python\ncondition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= self._grind_xl() or \\\n    (LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n     self.agent.character.role in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n     self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.HUNGRY and\n     self.agent.inventory.items.total_nutrition() == 0)\n```\n\nFor Healer, `role in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY` is False, so the second part is False. But the first part `experience_level >= self._grind_xl()` should trigger at XP 8 (since `_grind_xl` defaults to `GRIND_XL = 8` for Healer).\n\nHmm, but there's also this code after the condition check:\n\n```python\nif condition():\n    # ... switch to mines or go down\n    race = self.agent.character.race\n    mines_folk = MINES_FOLK_ROUTE and self._role_routes() and race in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF)\n    if self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL and race != Character.GNOME and \\\n            not mines_folk:\n        if PICK_HUNT_TURNS > 0 and self._role_routes() and race != Character.DWARF:\n            self._pick_hunt_start = self.agent.blstats.time\n            self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES\n        else:\n            self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n        continue\n```\n\nSo for a Healer-Gnome, `race != Character.GNOME` is False (since it IS gnome), so this whole block is skipped. Then it goes to:\n\n```python\nif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and self._pick_hunt_start is not None:\n    self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n    continue\nif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and mines_folk:\n    self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_MINES_END\n    continue\nself.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\ncontinue\n```\n\nSo for Healer-Gnome at BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL with XP >= 8, `condition()` is True, and then since race is GNOME, the special gnome handling is skipped, and it just increments the milestone to FIND_GNOMISH_MINES.\n\nOK, so the milestone progression seems OK for Healer-Gnome. Let me think about what else could be going wrong.\n\nLet me look at the `anger_peaceful_dwarf` strategy more carefully. This is important for getting a pick-axe from a peaceful dwarf in the Mines. The strategy checks:\n- Not gnome/dwarf\n- Not hallucinating/polymorphed\n- HP >= 80%\n- Not weak from hunger\n- Has a pick for digging\n\nFor Healer-Gnome, this would yield False immediately because `a.character.race not in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF)` is False (it IS gnome). So the anger_peaceful_dwarf strategy is skipped for gnomes, which is correct since gnomes have peaceful dwarves they don't need to anger.\n\nBut wait - for a Healer-Gnome, the bot should be taking the Mines folk route (walking peaceful dwarves to the pick-axe). Let me check if that's working...\n\nActually, looking at the code again, I think the issue might be more fundamental. Let me look at how the bot handles the early game.\n\nLet me re-examine the `global_strategy` method. It chains strategies with preemption. The order is:\n1. current_strategy().repeat() - the main milestone-based strategy\n2. solve_sokoban_strategy\n3. offer_corpses\n4. wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy\n5. cure_disease\n6. eat_corpses_from_ground\n7. follow_guard\n8. anger_peaceful_dwarf\n9. fight2\n10. engulfed_fight\n11. proactive_sleep_strategy\n12. emergency_strategy\n13. read_magic_mapping\n14. dig_down\n\nThe `current_strategy().repeat()` is the main driver. It cycles through milestones.\n\nLet me think about what might cause a score of 0.091 for Healer-Gnome specifically.\n\nActually, I realize I should just try running the bot and seeing what happens. But first, let me look at some key areas that might need improvement.\n\nLooking at the code more carefully, I notice a few things:\n\n1. The `elbereth_action` in `fight_heur.py` - this gives priority to engraving Elbereth when there are adjacent monsters. Elbereth is crucial for survival in NetHack.\n\n2. The `get_priorities` function in `fight_heur.py` - this determines action priorities. I see that `elbereth_action` and `wait_action` are added at the end.\n\n3. The `decide_what_to_pickup` function - this picks up items. For a Healer-Gnome, picking up the right items is important.\n\n4. The `get_best_ranged_set` and related inventory functions.\n\nLet me think about what specific improvement I could make...\n\nActually, let me re-read the task more carefully. It says:\n- \"Make ONE focused change that raises its score\"\n- \"Higher is better\" for BALROG progression\n- The bot currently scores 0.091\n- The identity is `hea-gno-neu-mal` (Healer-Gnome-Neutral-Male)\n- Per-seed detail is in `/refs/parent-eval.json` which has 15 rows (1 identity × 15 seeds)\n\nBut the /refs directory doesn't exist! Let me check if it's somewhere else or if I need to look at git more carefully.\n\nWait, looking at the task description again: \"Start with /refs/CONTEXT.md — it lists what's there: a pristine copy of this bot (parent/), its per-seed results (parent-eval.json), and other changes that were tried with the score each reached (attempts.md, with their code under attempts/).\"\n\nBut these files don't exist in the workspace. Maybe they're supposed to be there but aren't, or maybe they're in git history. Let me check git.","time":{"start":1790514346927,"end":1790514400418}}}
