{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790514822950,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e2ffa0a9001dL0Nr7VY86jdZG","messageID":"msg_0e2ff9d830017r4tpocNAUIPHQ","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have the per-seed results for Healer-Gnome-Neutral-Male. Let me analyze:\n\n- Seed 8: 0.554 depth 27 - this is the best run, killed by invisible titan at Dlvl:27\n- Seed 7: 0.126 depth 10 - killed by bolt of lightning at Dlvl:10\n- Seed 0: 0.117 depth 6 - killed by gargoyle at Xp:9\n- Seed 4: 0.117 depth 4 - killed by soldier ant at Xp:9\n- Seed 10: 0.098 depth 9 - killed by owlbear at Dlvl:9\n- Seed 1: 0.075 depth 4 - killed by Woodland-elf at Xp:8\n- Seed 3: 0.037 depth 1 - killed by cave spider at Xp:6\n- Seed 9: 0.037 depth 1 - killed by wererat at Xp:6\n- Seed 11: 0.051 depth 3 - killed by rothe at Xp:7\n- Seed 12: 0.024 depth 1 - killed by hobbit at Xp:4\n- Seed 13: 0.037 depth 1 - killed by little dog at Xp:6\n- Seed 14: 0.021 depth 1 - killed by hobbit at Xp:3\n- Seed 5: 0.021 depth 1 - killed by brown mold at Xp:3\n- Seed 6: 0.029 depth 1 - killed by dwarf zombie at Xp:5\n- Seed 12: 0.024 depth 1 - killed by hobbit at Xp:4\n\nThe scores range from 0.021 to 0.554, with mean probably around 0.091 (as stated in the task).\n\nKey observations:\n1. Seed 8 is a clear outlier at 0.554 - it got to Dlvl 27\n2. Most runs die very early (depth 1-6) \n3. The bot frequently dies to early-game monsters (spiders, wererats, brown mold, hobbit, dwarf zombie, little dog)\n4. Some die to mid-game monsters (gargoyle, soldier ant, Woodland-elf, owlbear, rothe)\n5. Only one seed (8) gets very deep (27)\n\nThe main issues seem to be:\n1. Early game survival - dying to low-level monsters\n2. Not getting out of Dlvl 1 early enough\n3. Not descending to deeper levels consistently\n\nLet me think about what specific improvement to make. Looking at the code, several things could be improved:\n\n1. **Elbereth engraving** - The bot needs to engrave Elbereth early for survival. Looking at `elbereth_action` in `fight_heur.py`, it checks if the bot can engrave and if there are adjacent monsters. But the key question is: does the bot actually engrave Elbereth early enough?\n\n2. **Dlvl 1 grind** - The bot needs to leave the Dlvl 1 grind at the right time. For Healer-Gnome, the `_grind_xl()` defaults to 8, and Healer is NOT in `ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY`. So the bot might stay on Dlvl 1 grinding XP even when hungry, which could be suboptimal.\n\n3. **Pick-axe hunting** - For non-gnome/dwarf roles, getting a pick-axe from angering peaceful dwarves is important. But Healer-Gnome is a gnome, so it takes the peaceful Mines route instead.\n\n4. **Spellcasting** - Healers don't start with offensive spells, but they can pray for healing.\n\n5. **Inventory management** - Picking up the right items, especially food and healing items.\n\nLet me think about the most impactful change...\n\nLooking at the deaths:\n- Many deaths happen at Dlvl 1-3, early game\n- Brown mold and dwarf zombie kills suggest the bot is taking too much damage\n- Getting killed by \"little dog\" and \"hobbit\" at Dlvl 1 is concerning - these should be manageable\n\nA key improvement would be to ensure the bot engravings Elbereth early. Elbereth is the most important survival tool in NetHack - engraving \"elbereth\" on the floor gives significant protection against monsters.\n\nLet me check if the bot currently engraves Elbereth. Looking at the code:\n\nIn `fight_heur.py`, `elbereth_action` returns priorities for engraving Elbereth when there are adjacent monsters. But this is only called during combat.\n\nIn `exploration_logic.py`, `explore1` has `open_neighbor_doors` but I don't see explicit Elbereth engraving.\n\nIn `global_logic.py`, there's `identify_items_on_altar` strategy but that's for identifying items on an altar, not specifically for engraving Elbereth.\n\nWait, let me search for \"elbereth\" in the codebase.","time":