{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790514966789,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e300108a001EmHUALkQU43r0D","messageID":"msg_0e3000d460015jtcjfaDyS1nM8","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I see the `emergency_strategy` in agent.py. The key part is at lines 1635-1651 - this is the Elbereth \"last resort\" that only triggers when the Healer is at critical HP (< max/5 or < 5) with every other emergency option exhausted.\n\nThe comment says: \"hypothesis: many runs die in melee at low XP (Xp5-7) across all four identities. This Elbereth last resort sits at the very bottom of emergency_strategy -- below the healing cast, healing potion, fruit juice and prayer -- so it only fires when the Healer is at critical HP (< max/5 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a near-certain death.\"\n\nSo the Elbereth engraving is a last-resort measure. The problem is it only triggers when the Healer is already near death. We need to engage Elbereth EARLIER to prevent deaths in the first place.\n\nLet me also look at the `proactive_sleep_strategy` - it skips gnomes (!!) because \"the gnome runs' whole score comes from a few RNG-fragile deep dives that must stay byte-identical\". This is important - for Healer-Gnome, the proactive sleep strategy is disabled.\n\nLet me think about what specific improvement to make. The key issues for Healer-Gnome based on the per-seed analysis:\n\n1. Early deaths (depth 1-3) to weak monsters (brown mold, dwarf zombie, little dog, hobbit) - these should be preventable\n2. The bot doesn't seem to be engraving Elbereth early enough\n3. The proactive_sleep_strategy is disabled for gnomes\n\nLet me think about a focused change. The task says \"Make ONE focused change, marked with a `# hypothesis: …` comment saying what you expect it to improve.\"\n\nLooking at the code and the death patterns, I think a good focused change would be to:\n\n**Engrave Elbereth proactively, not just as a last resort.**\n\nThe current code only engraves Elbereth when near death (critical HP). Instead, we should engrave Elbereth much earlier - as soon as the bot is on a new level and can safely do so. Elbereth is the most important survival tool in NetHack, and engraving it early prevents many deaths from weak monsters.\n\nBut wait - the task says \"Don't game the score: no branching on seed fingerprints, no exploiting scorer/NLE quirks — those don't generalize.\" So I need to make a genuine improvement, not a cheat.\n\nLet me think about what would be a legitimate improvement:\n\n1. **Engrave Elbereth earlier** - The current code only engraves at < 20% HP or < 5 HP. If we move this to a higher threshold (e.g., < 50% HP or < 20 HP), the bot would engrave Elbereth earlier and survive more often. But is this \"gaming\" the score? Engraving Elbereth is a legitimate NetHack strategy - the code already has it as a last-resort, just moving the threshold earlier is a genuine strategy improvement.\n\n2. **Fix proactive_sleep_strategy for gnomes** - Currently it yields False immediately for gnomes. If we enable it for gnomes with appropriate adjustments, it could help them survive early game.\n\n3. **Improve the Dlvl 1 grind exit** - For Healer specifically, ensuring the bot leaves the grind at the right time.\n\nLet me look more carefully at the proactive_sleep_strategy and the emergency_strategy to understand which change would be most impactful.\n\nActually, let me re-read the proactive_sleep_strategy comment: \"the gnome runs' whole score comes from a few RNG-fragile deep dives that must stay byte-identical, whereas humans -- who have no deep runs to protect and drag the average down -- are exactly who this rescue is for.\"\n\nThis suggests the proactive sleep was intentionally disabled for gnomes to preserve byte-identical runs. But if we're trying to improve the score, maybe we should reconsider this.\n\nLet me think about what change would be most impactful and yet still \"focused\"...\n\nActually, I think the most impactful change would be to **engrave Elbereth earlier in the game**, not just as a last resort at < 5 HP. The current threshold is very low (< 1/5 max HP or < 5), which means the bot only engraves when it's already on the brink of death. If we raise the threshold, the bot would engrave Elbereth much earlier, preventing many deaths.\n\nBut I need to be careful about how I do this. Let me look at the exact condition again:\n\n```python\nif self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth' and self.can_engrave() and \\\n        (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 5 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):\n```\n\nThis triggers when HP is less than 20% of max OR less than 5. For a Healer at XL 1-2 with max HP around 15-25, this means HP < 3-5. That's very late in the game.\n\nA reasonable change would be to also trigger when the bot is weakened but not near death, or to add a condition based on the number of visible monsters or some other survival indicator.\n\nBut wait - I need to think about this more carefully. The comment says this is intended as a \"last resort\" that only fires when \"every other emergency option already exhausted.\" If I move it earlier, it might interfere with the normal game flow.\n\nLet me look at another approach. Maybe I should focus on the `proactive_sleep_strategy` for gnomes. The current code completely disables it for gnomes. If I enable it with appropriate modifications, it could help gnome Healers survive early game fights.\n\nActually, let me re-read the proactive_sleep_strategy more carefully. It uses a wand of sleep proactively - when a threatening monster is 2-4 tiles away on a straight line, zap it with sleep first, then let fight2 kill it while it's helpless. This is actually a really good strategy for Healer-Gnome since:\n- Healers start with limited combat options\n- Sleep wand is a good early weapon\n- Putting monsters to sleep before combat prevents taking damage\n\nThe reason it's disabled for gnomes is to preserve byte-identical runs with the parent bot. But if we're trying to improve the score, enabling it (with appropriate adjustments to stay somewhat byte-identical) could help.\n\nLet me think about what specific, focused change to make...\n\nActually, I just realized something. Let me re-read the task description: \"Make ONE focused change that raises its score.\" and \"Keep the make_agent() → reset() / act() contract intact and make sure the code imports cleanly.\"\n\nThe change needs to be in the strategy code in the `autoascend/` package, not the `arena_adapter.py` glue.\n\nLet me think about what change would be most impactful. Based on the per-seed analysis:\n\n- Many seeds die very early (depth 1-3) to weak monsters\n- The bot rarely gets past Dlvl 10\n- Only one seed (8) gets very deep (27)\n\nThe common theme is early game survival. The bot needs to:\n1. Survive the early game (Dlvl 1-3)\n2. Get out of the Dlvl 1 grind\n3. Descend to deeper levels\n\nLet me consider changing the Elbereth engraving threshold. Currently it's at < 1/5 max HP or < 5 HP. If I change it to something like < 1/2 max HP or < 15 HP, the bot would engrave Elbereth much earlier, which should significantly improve survival rates.\n\nBut I need to make sure this is a \"focused\" change and not something that games the score. Engraving Elbereth earlier is a legitimate NetHack strategy - the earlier you have Elbereth engraved, the more monsters it deters.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the code one more time. The Elbereth engraving in `emergency_strategy` is at the BOTTOM of the strategy chain, preempted by many other strategies. It only fires when ALL other options are exhausted. So even if I change the threshold, it would still only trigger as a last resort, just at a less-critical HP level.\n\nLet me think about another approach. What about modifying the `proactive_sleep_strategy` to work for gnomes (with some adjustment)? The current code just yields False for gnomes. If I enable it with a reasonable adjustment (e.g., only for non-healthy gnomes, or with a different RNG approach), it could help.\n\nActually, I just realized something important. Let me re-read the proactive_sleep_strategy comment more carefully:\n\n\"the gnome runs' whole score comes from a few RNG-fragile deep dives that must stay byte-identical, whereas humans -- who have no deep runs to protect and drag the average down -- are exactly who this rescue is for.\"\n\nThis says gnome runs get their score from deep dives, and the proactive sleep would risk breaking byte-identicity. But if we're trying to improve the score, maybe we should enable it with some adjustment.\n\nOK, let me just decide on a change. I'll go with modifying the Elbereth engraving threshold in `emergency_strategy` to trigger at a higher HP threshold. Specifically, I'll change the condition from:\n\n```python\nself.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 5 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5\n```\n\nto something like:\n\n```python\nself.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 2 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 15\n```\n\nThis would cause the bot to engrave Elbereth much earlier in the game, which should significantly improve survival rates, especially in the early game where many deaths occur.\n\nWait, but I need to be more careful. Let me look at what the actual impact would be. The Elbereth engraving in `emergency_strategy` is a \"last resort\" that triggers when the Healer is near death. If I raise the threshold, it will trigger earlier, but still only when other options are exhausted.\n\nActually, I realize I should look at this from a different angle. Let me check what the parent bot (before any improvements) does, and what specific changes have been made in previous commits.\n\nActually, let me just go with a change and see if it works. I'll modify the Elbereth engraving threshold to be less aggressive (higher HP threshold), which should help the bot survive longer and get deeper into the dungeon.\n\nActually wait - let me reconsider. The task mentions the current score is 0.091, but my test run showed 0.117 for one seed. Let me re-check...\n\nActually the 0.091 is the \"overall\" mean across all identities, while 0.117 is just for hea-gno-neu-mal on one seed. The task says to improve the bot that plays `hea-gno-neu-mal`.\n\nLet me make my change and test it. I'll modify the Elbereth engraving threshold.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me think about this more carefully. The `emergency_strategy` is just one part of the overall strategy. Let me look at what other changes might be more impactful.\n\nLooking at the deaths again:\n- Seed 2: died of starvation at Dlvl 1, Xp 4 - the bot didn't manage food well\n- Seed 5: killed by brown mold at Dlvl 1, Xp 3 - early game damage\n- Seed 6: killed by dwarf zombie at Dlvl 1, Xp 5 - early game damage\n- Seed 12: killed by hobbit at Dlvl 1, Xp 4 - early game damage\n- Seed 13: killed by little dog at Dlvl 1, Xp 6 - early game damage\n- Seed 14: killed by hobbit at Dlvl 1, Xp 3 - early game damage\n\nMany early deaths. Elbereth would help prevent many of these (hobbits, little dogs, brown mold are all deterred by Elbereth).\n\nLet me also consider: the `proactive_sleep_strategy` is disabled for gnomes. If I enable it, it could help gnome Healers avoid early melee combat by putting monsters to sleep first.\n\nOK, I've been going back and forth. Let me just make a decision and implement it.\n\nMy final decision: **Modify the Elbereth engraving threshold in `emergency_strategy` to trigger at a higher HP threshold.** Specifically, I'll change the condition from `hitpoints < 1/5 * max_hitpoints or hitpoints < 5` to `hitpoints < 1/2 * max_hitpoints or hitpoints < 15`. This will cause the bot to engrave Elbereth much earlier in the game, which should significantly improve early game survival.\n\nWait, actually I want to make sure this is a \"focused\" change. Let me re-read the task: \"Make ONE focused change, marked with a `# hypothesis: …` comment saying what you expect it to improve.\"\n\nOK, let me implement the change. I'll modify the Elbereth engraving condition.\n\nActually, one more thought. Let me look at what specific HP values trigger the current condition for a Healer. A Healer at XL 1 has max HP around 15 (constitution 10-11 gives about 15 HP). At XL 2, maybe 17-18. At XL 3, maybe 20-22. At XL 4, maybe 23-25. At XL 5, maybe 26-28.\n\nWith the current condition `hitpoints < 1/5 * max_hitpoints or hitpoints < 5`:\n- At XL 1 with max HP 15: triggers at HP < 3 or HP < 5, so HP <= 4\n- At XL 5 with max HP 28: triggers at HP < 5.6 or HP < 5, so HP <= 5\n\nSo the current condition only triggers when the Healer is already very close to death. Changing to `hitpoints < 1/2 * max_hitpoints or hitpoints < 15`:\n- At XL 1 with max HP 15: triggers at HP < 7.5 or HP < 15, so HP <= 7\n- At XL 5 with max HP 28: triggers at HP < 14 or HP < 15, so HP <= 14\n\nThis would cause engraving at roughly half health, which is much earlier and should prevent many deaths.\n\nLet me implement this change.\n\nActually, wait. I want to make sure the change is correct and won't break things. Let me re-read the full emergency_strategy context.\n\nLooking at the code again, the emergency_strategy is called from global_strategy with the lowest priority (last in the preempt list). It's the very last strategy to be tried. So even if I change the threshold, it will still only fire when all other strategies have been exhausted, just at a less-critical HP level.\n\nOK, let me make the change. I'll modify the condition in emergency_strategy to raise the Elbereth engraving threshold.","time":{"start":1790514827402,"end":1790514966782}}}
