{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790518589018,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e3394798001rIxSKVL1R8gciD","messageID":"msg_0e33944cb0017W2lPxi2S5zpop","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I see! There's already an `emergency_sleep` strategy in the agent that uses the sleep wand, but it's scoped to non-gnome Healers (the condition `self.character.race != self.character.GNOME`). This is the same reason the proactive_sleep_strategy was disabled for gnomes.\n\nThe emergency_sleep strategy triggers at `HP < 1/3 * max_hitpoints or HP < 8` - i.e., when the Healer is in crisis mode. It zaps the sleep wand at an adjacent monster.\n\nThe proactive_sleep_strategy I modified would use the sleep wand proactively (before combat, when monsters are 2-4 tiles away), but the Healer might not start with a sleep wand in their inventory.\n\nLet me check what wand Healers start with. In NetHack, the Healer's starting inventory typically includes a wand of healing, not a wand of sleep. Let me verify.\n\nActually, looking at the emergency_sleep code, it searches for a wand of sleep in the inventory: `for item in flatten_items(self.inventory.items): if item.is_wand() and item.is_unambiguous() and item.object.name == 'sleep'`. If the Healer doesn't start with a sleep wand, this would just yield False.\n\nLet me check what the Healer starts with by running a quick observation.","time":{"start":1790518577048,"end":1790518589003}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790518589053,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-5a75aa21-3ab8-4c73-9293-09f588f0b333","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport json\n# Quick check: what does the Healer start with?\nd = json.load(open('/tmp/eval_sleep1.json'))\n# Let me just check the first seed's details\nprint(json.dumps(d[0], indent=2)[:500])\n\""},"output":"{\n  \"trajectory_id\": 0,\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"progress\": 0.11704996473565571,\n  \"ascended\": false,\n  \"steps\": 40743,\n  \"turns\": 29870,\n  \"max_depth\": 6,\n  \"end_status\": \"1\",\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"wall_seconds\": 100.221139,\n  \"character\": \"hea-gno-neu-mal\",\n  \"milestone\": \"Xp:9\",\n  \"cause_of_death\": \"killed by a gargoyle\"\n}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"trajectory_id\": 0,\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"progress\": 0.11704996473565571,\n  \"ascended\": false,\n  \"steps\": 40743,\n  \"turns\": 29870,\n  \"max_depth\": 6,\n  \"end_status\": \"1\",\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"wall_seconds\": 100.221139,\n  \"character\": \"hea-gno-neu-mal\",\n  \"milestone\": \"Xp:9\",\n  \"cause_of_death\": \"killed by a gargoyle\"\n}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport json\n# Quick check: what does the Healer start with?\nd = json.load(open('/tmp/eval_sleep1.json'))\n# Let me just check the first seed's details\nprint(json.dumps(d[0], indent=2)[:500])\n\"","time":{"start":1790518589012,"end":1790518589051}},"id":"prt_0e339764d001GBjNGnnDg8Ac9g","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","messageID":"msg_0e33944cb0017W2lPxi2S5zpop"}}
