{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790518610254,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e3397b200016Pj61EVWqXF4Wv","messageID":"msg_0e33976f2001QYSxFhNREeYogZ","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"The results don't show the inventory. Let me check if Healers start with a sleep wand by looking at the game's starting inventory or the agent's item setup.\n\nActually, let me just check if the Healer start with a sleep wand by looking at NetHack's standard starting inventories. In NetHack 3.6.x, the Healer role starts with:\n- A wand of healing (un charged) \n- A scalpel\n- A stethoscope\n- Some food\n- A tinning kit\n- etc.\n\nThey don't typically start with a wand of sleep. The sleep wand is something you find during the game.\n\nSo the proactive_sleep_strategy would yield False because there's no sleep wand in the starting inventory. The emergency_sleep strategy has the same issue - it also searches for a sleep wand.\n\nWait, but the emergency_sleep IS in the global_strategy preempt list (from global_logic.py line 890-914). Let me check if it actually fires...\n\nActually, looking at the global_strategy in global_logic.py, the strategies are preempted in order. The emergency_strategy (which contains the emergency_sleep) is near the end of the preempt chain. But the emergency_sleep only triggers at low HP (< 1/3 max or < 8), which is the crisis mode.\n\nFor the proactive_sleep_strategy I modified, it would need a sleep wand to work. Since Healers don't start with one, the strategy would yield False at the `if sleep_wand is None: yield False` check.\n\nSo modifying the proactive_sleep_strategy to remove the gnome check doesn't help if Healers don't start with a sleep wand. I need a different approach.\n\nLet me think about this differently. What are some genuine, focused changes that would improve the Healer-Gnome score?\n\n1. **Elbereth engraving earlier** - I already tried this and got mixed results due to RNG sensitivity.\n\n2. **Better food management** - Many seeds die of starvation (seeds 2, 4, 6, 7, 8, 12, 14). If the bot manages food better, it would survive longer.\n\n3. **Better early game combat** - The bot dies to weak monsters (hobbit, little dog, cave spider, brown mold). Elbereth would help, but the RNG-sensitive threshold change had mixed results.\n\n4. **Better level exploration** - The bot needs to find stairs and descend rather than grinding on Dlvl 1.\n\nLet me look at the food management. The `proactive_sleep_strategy` wasn't helpful because Healers don't start with a sleep wand. But maybe there are other food-related improvements.\n\nActually, let me re-examine the Elbereth change. The mean score went from 0.0912 to 0.0750 for 10 seeds, but with significant variation:\n- Seed 0: 0.117 → 0.426 (+0.309, huge improvement)\n- Seed 3: 0.037 → 0.161 (+0.124, huge improvement)\n- Seed 9: 0.037 → 0.126 (+0.089, improvement)\n- Seed 8: 0.554 → 0.000 (catastrophic failure)\n- Seeds 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7: worsened or no change\n\nThe problem is that seed 8 was the best run and my change broke it. Let me think about why.\n\nSeed 8 got to depth 27 with progress 0.554, killed by an invisible titan. This is a very deep run. The Elbereth engraving change probably altered the RNG sequence enough that this run no longer achieved the same depth.\n\nWhat if I take a less aggressive approach to the Elbereth change? Instead of changing the threshold from 1/5 to 1/2, what if I add an additional early-engraving condition, or change the threshold more subtly?\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole approach. The task says \"Make ONE focused change.\" Let me think about what single change would be most likely to raise the score consistently.\n\nLooking at the death causes:\n- Many early deaths to weak monsters that Elbereth would deter\n- Some deaths to starvation\n- Some deaths to mid-game monsters\n\nThe most common theme is early game survival. Elbereth is the most important tool for early game survival in NetHack. The current code only engraves it as a last resort at critical HP.\n\nWhat if I modify the Elbereth engraving to also trigger when the bot is on a new level and hasn't engraved yet? For example, \"engrave Elbereth on the first level visit if no Elbereth is already engraved\"? This would ensure Elbereth is engraved early in every run, without being as RNG-sensitive as changing the HP threshold.\n\nBut I need to be careful about how to implement this. Let me look at the code flow.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach entirely. What about modifying the `current_strategy` in `global_logic.py` to ensure the bot leaves the Dlvl 1 grind earlier? Looking at the condition:\n\n```python\ncondition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= self._grind_xl() or \\\n    (LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n     self.agent.character.role in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n     self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.HUNGRY and\n     self.agent.inventory.items.total_nutrition() == 0)\n```\n\nFor Healer, `role in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY` is False (Healer is not in the set). So the bot will only leave the grind when `experience_level >= self._grind_xl()`. For Healer, `_grind_xl()` defaults to `GRIND_XL = 8`.\n\nBut wait, looking at the code after the condition check:\n\n```python\nif condition():\n    # ... switch to mines or go down\n    race = self.agent.character.race\n    mines_folk = MINES_FOLK_ROUTE and self._role_routes() and race in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF)\n    if self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL and race != Character.GNOME and \\\n            not mines_folk:\n        if PICK_HUNT_TURNS > 0 and self._role_routes() and race != Character.DWARF:\n            self._pick_hunt_start = self.agent.blstats.time\n            self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES\n        else:\n            self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n        continue\n```\n\nFor Healer-Gnome, `race != Character.GNOME` is False (it IS gnome), so this whole block is skipped. Then:\n\n```python\nif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and self._pick_hunt_start is not None:\n    self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n    continue\nif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and mines_folk:\n    self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_MINES_END\n    continue\nself.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\ncontinue\n```\n\nSo for Healer-Gnome at BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL with XP >= 8, the milestone just increments to FIND_GNOMISH_MINES. Then the bot goes to the Gnomish Mines.\n\nOK, the milestone progression seems fine. Let me think about other changes.\n\nActually, let me go back to the Elbereth change. The key issue was that it broke seed 8 (the best run). What if I make the Elbereth threshold change less aggressive? Instead of 1/2, use 1/3 or some other value?\n\nLet me test with a 1/3 threshold.","time":{"start":1790518590240,"end":1790518610247}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790518617437,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-814817ea-8cc7-4354-87c4-588aa54986b7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/autoascend/agent.py","newString":"# hypothesis: many runs die in melee at low XP (Xp5-7) across all four identities. This\n        # Elbereth last resort sits at the very bottom of emergency_strategy -- below the healing\n        # cast, healing potion, fruit juice and prayer -- so it only fires when the Healer is at\n        # critical HP (< max/3 or < 8) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n        # near-certain death. Engraving Elbereth in the dust scares off the common early attackers\n        # (most animals, humanoids, etc.), and waiting on it lets HP regenerate, converting otherwise\n        # terminal combat deaths into survival == more XP == more score. Because it triggers only in\n        # this otherwise-fatal, resource-empty state, resourced/healthy runs never reach it.\n        if self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth' and self.can_engrave() and \\\n                (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 3 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 8):","oldString":"# hypothesis: many runs die in melee at low XP (Xp5-7) across all four identities. This\n        # Elbereth last resort sits at the very bottom of emergency_strategy -- below the healing\n        # cast, healing potion, fruit juice and prayer -- so it only fires when the Healer is at\n        # critical HP (< max/5 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n        # near-certain death. Engraving Elbereth in the dust scares off the common early attackers\n        # (most animals, humanoids, etc.), and waiting on it lets HP regenerate, converting otherwise\n        # terminal combat deaths into survival == more XP == more score. Because it triggers only in\n        # this otherwise-fatal, resource-empty state, resourced/healthy runs never reach it.\n        if self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth' and self.can_engrave() and \\\n                (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 5 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n+++ /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n@@ -1634,15 +1634,15 @@\n \n # hypothesis: many runs die in melee at low XP (Xp5-7) across all four identities. This\n # Elbereth last resort sits at the very bottom of emergency_strategy -- below the healing\n # cast, healing potion, fruit juice and prayer -- so it only fires when the Healer is at\n-# critical HP (< max/5 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n+# critical HP (< max/3 or < 8) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n # near-certain death. Engraving Elbereth in the dust scares off the common early attackers\n # (most animals, humanoids, etc.), and waiting on it lets HP regenerate, converting otherwise\n # terminal combat deaths into survival == more XP == more score. Because it triggers only in\n # this otherwise-fatal, resource-empty state, resourced/healthy runs never reach it.\n if self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth' and self.can_engrave() and \\\n-        (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 5 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):\n+        (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 3 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 8):\n     yield True\n     self.engrave('Elbereth')\n     for _ in range(8):\n         if self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth':\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/autoascend/agent.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/autoascend/agent.py\n===================================================================\n-