{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790518762391,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e33bc758001VsIop3BfkvUS12","messageID":"msg_0e33bc4f6001V7rbuowsJlMmFO","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting - with the 1/3 threshold, the results are identical to the old baseline for these 5 seeds. The Elbereth engraving isn't triggering at all, or it's triggering but having no effect on these particular seeds.\n\nThis makes sense - the Elbereth engraving in `emergency_strategy` is a last-resort strategy that only triggers when ALL other options are exhausted AND the Healer is at critical HP. For these seeds, the bot might not reach that state, or the Elbereth engraving might not be effective in preventing the specific deaths.\n\nThe problem is that the Elbereth engraving is so far down in the strategy chain (last resort) that it rarely triggers. And when it does trigger, it might not prevent the specific death cause.\n\nLet me think about this differently. Maybe I need a change that's more fundamentally impactful. Let me look at the code structure again and think about what change would be most impactful.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about what the real bottleneck is for Healer-Gnome. Looking at the per-seed results:\n\n- 15 seeds, mean 0.091\n- Best: seed 8 at 0.554 (depth 27)\n- Worst: seeds 2, 5, 12, 14 at 0.021 (depth 1)\n- Most seeds die at depth 1-6\n\nThe key question is: why does the bot die so early? Let me look at the specific deaths more carefully.\n\nFrom the 15 seeds:\n- Seed 0: gargoyle at Xp:9, Dlvl:6\n- Seed 1: Woodland-elf at Xp:8, Dlvl:4\n- Seed 2: starvation at Xp:4, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 3: cave spider at Xp:6, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 4: soldier ant at Xp:9, Dlvl:4\n- Seed 5: brown mold at Xp:3, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 6: dwarf zombie at Xp:5, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 7: bolt of lightning at Dlvl:10\n- Seed 8: invisible titan at Dlvl:27 (the outlier)\n- Seed 9: wererat at Xp:6, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 10: owlbear at Dlvl:9\n- Seed 11: rothe at Xp:7, Dlvl:3\n- Seed 12: hobbit at Xp:4, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 13: little dog at Xp:6, Dlvl:1\n- Seed 14: hobbit at Xp:3, Dlvl:1\n\nMany deaths are from:\n- Early game (Dlvl 1): brown mold, dwarf zombie, cave spider, wererat, hobbit, little dog\n- Mid game: gargoyle, Woodland-elf, soldier ant, rothe, owlbear\n\nThe early deaths (Dlvl 1) to weak monsters are the most concerning. These should be preventable with better play.\n\nLet me think about what specific improvement would help with these early deaths...\n\n1. **Elbereth engraving** - Would prevent most of these deaths, but the last-resort threshold is too late\n\n2. **Proactive sleep** - Healer doesn't start with sleep wand\n\n3. **Better prayer usage** - Healers can pray for healing\n\n4. **Better inventory management** - Picking up food, healing items\n\n5. **Better level exploration** - Getting out of Dlvl 1 faster\n\nLet me look at the prayer code. The `critically_low_hp` and `is_safe_to_pray` functions control prayer usage. Looking at `critically_low_hp`:\n\n```python\ndef critically_low_hp(self):\n    hp, max_hp, level = self.blstats.hitpoints, self.blstats.max_hitpoints, self.blstats.experience_level\n    max_hp = min(max_hp, 15 * level)\n    divisor = 5 if level <= 5 else 6 if level <= 13 else 7 if level <= 21 else 8 if level <= 29 else 9\n    if not PRAY_AT_EXACT_THRESHOLD:\n        divisor, max_hp = 7, self.blstats.max_hitpoints\n    return hp <= 5 or hp * divisor <= max_hp\n```\n\nAnd `is_safe_to_pray`:\n```python\ndef is_safe_to_pray(self, limit=500):\n    if self.prayer_failed:\n        return False\n    return (\n            (self.last_prayer_turn is None and self.blstats.time > 110) or\n            (self.last_prayer_turn is not None and self.blstats.time - self.last_prayer_turn > limit)\n    )\n```\n\nThe prayer is only used at crisis HP or after a long timeout. For a Healer, prayer is a important healing source. But the current code only prays at very low HP.\n\nWhat if I modify the prayer threshold to pray earlier? This could help Healers survive longer by topping up HP before they reach critical state.\n\nBut I need to be careful about the prayer timeout and the \"god angry\" mechanic. The `is_safe_to_pray` function already has a timeout check.\n\nLet me think about a focused change related to prayer. Currently, the Healer prays only when:\n1. At crisis HP (hp <= 5 or hp * divisor <= max_hp)\n2. After a long enough timeout since last prayer\n\nWhat if I modify the prayer to also trigger when the Healer is below half HP, not just critical HP? This would allow the Healer to pray more frequently and maintain HP above dangerous levels.\n\nBut wait, the task says \"Don't game the score: no branching on seed fingerprints, no exploiting scorer/NLE quirks — those don't generalize.\" Modifying prayer thresholds could be seen as exploiting the scorer, since prayer is a powerful healing tool in NetHack.\n\nActually, prayer is a legitimate NetHack mechanic, and using it more frequently is a genuine strategy improvement. The key is to make the change in a way that generalizes across seeds.\n\nLet me look at the prayer code one more time and think about a reasonable change.\n\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. Let me look at what happens when the bot reaches the Gnomish Mines (since Healer-Gnome takes the Mines folk route). The Mines can be dangerous for a Healer who doesn't have a digging tool.\n\nWait, for Healer-Gnome, the bot should be walking peaceful dwarves in the Mines to get a pick-axe, then digging down. Let me check if the anger_peaceful_dwarf strategy is relevant... No, for gnomes, this strategy yields False immediately because `a.character.race not in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF)` is False.\n\nFor gnomes, the bot takes the peaceful Mines route. But the exploration and navigation in the Mines might need improvement.\n\nActually, let me re-examine the proactive_sleep_strategy change I made earlier. Even though Healers don't start with a sleep wand, maybe the strategy still has value if the bot finds a sleep wand during the game. But that would be very rare and RNG-sensitive.\n\nOK, let me try a prayer-related change. I'll modify the prayer threshold to allow praying at a higher HP threshold. This is a genuine NetHack improvement - Healers praying more frequently should survive better.\n\nLet me look at the prayer code in detail.","time":{"start":1790518740824,"end":1790518762384}}}
