points` at line 1602. This means hunger prayer triggers when HP is less than half max HP. This is a much more reasonable threshold!\n\nSo the hunger prayer already has a better threshold (HP < 50%), but the major trouble prayer has a very low threshold (HP < ~20% at low XL).\n\nWhat if I modify `critically_low_hp` to use a higher threshold, similar to the hunger prayer? This would allow the Healer to pray at higher HP, which should prevent many deaths.\n\nBut wait, looking at line 1602: `self.blstats.hitpoints * 2 < self.blstats.max_hitpoints` - this is already in the `hunger_prayer_due` check, not in `critically_low_hp`. The `critically_low_hp` has its own divisor-based threshold.\n\nLet me think about what change to make. I could modify `critically_low_hp` to use a fixed threshold instead of the divisor-based one. For example, change it to return True when `hp <= 8` or `hp * 3 <= max_hp` or similar.\n\nActually, looking at the comment on lines 1540-1548:\n```python\n# hypothesis: the weak Healers die mid-grind because the emergency prayer only fires at\n# HP < max/5 (or /6) or HP < 6 -- so low that a single hard hit (mumak, soldier ant, magic\n# missile, rothe, ...) drops them from a seemingly-safe HP straight to dead, skipping the\n# window entirely. Raise the crisis threshold to match the potion threshold (HP < max/3 or\n# HP < 8) so prayer -- the reliable full-heal backstop once potions are spent -- kicks in\n# with real margin. Games here are short (death by Xp5-8), so this rarely spends the ~once-\n# per-1000-turn prayer more than once, and surviving a hit beats starving 500 turns later.\n# Since score is essentially a function of experience level, more survival == more XP == more\n# score across all four Healer identities.\n```\n\nThis comment already recognizes the problem: \"the emergency prayer only fires at HP < max/5 (or /6) or HP < 6 -- so low that a single hard hit drops them from seemingly-safe HP straight to dead.\" The suggested fix is \"Raise the crisis threshold to match the potion threshold (HP < max/3 or HP < 8)\".\n\nBut this comment is about the `critically_low_hp` function, and it seems like this fix hasn't been applied yet (the code still has the old threshold). Or maybe it was applied in a different commit.\n\nWait, looking at the code again, `PRAY_AT_EXACT_THRESHOLD = True` (line 20), and the `critically_low_hp` function uses the divisor-based threshold. The comment suggests raising the threshold to `HP < max/3 or HP < 8`, but the code still has the old divisor-based threshold.\n\nSo my change could be to modify `critically_low_hp` to use the higher threshold. Let me do that.\n\nBut I need to be careful. The `critically_low_hp` function is used in two places:\n1. The major trouble prayer check at line 1607: `self.is_safe_to_pray(500) and self.critically_low_hp()`\n2. Some other place (maybe the emergency_sleep strategy)\n\nLet me check where else `critically_low_hp` is used.","time":{"start":1790518935591,"end":1790518965470}}}
