{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790518995971,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e33f40cd0019O3Wq5PjINFdCt","messageID":"msg_0e33f3e24001XEZ0oMcR69p71J","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I see the full picture. The `critically_low_hp()` function is used in two places:\n\n1. Line 1607: The major trouble prayer check in `update()`: `self.is_safe_to_pray(500) and self.critically_low_hp()`\n2. Line 1827: The dig strategy in some other method: `self.critically_low_hp() and self.is_safe_to_pray(500)`\n\nAnd at line 1831-1834, there's already a check for potion usage at `hp < max_hp / 3 or hp < 8` - this is the \"potion threshold\" mentioned in the comment at lines 1540-1548.\n\nSo the code already has the concept that `hp < max/3 or hp < 8` is the threshold for using healing items (potions). But `critically_low_hp` uses a divisor-based threshold that's much stricter at low XL.\n\nMy change: I'll modify `critically_low_hp` to use the same threshold as the potion check: `hp < max_hp / 3 or hp < 8`. This is the change suggested in the comment at lines 1540-1548.\n\nWait, but looking at the current `critically_low_hp`:\n```python\ndef critically_low_hp(self):\n    hp, max_hp, level = self.blstats.hitpoints, self.blstats.max_hitpoints, self.blstats.experience_level\n    max_hp = min(max_hp, 15 * level)\n    divisor = 5 if level <= 5 else 6 if level <= 13 else 7 if level <= 21 else 8 if level <= 29 else 9\n    if not PRAY_AT_EXACT_THRESHOLD:\n        divisor, max_hp = 7, self.blstats.max_hitpoints\n    return hp <= 5 or hp * divisor <= max_hp\n```\n\nWith `PRAY_AT_EXACT_THRESHOLD = True`:\n- At XL 1: max_hp = min(max_hitpoints, 15), divisor = 5. Returns True when hp <= 5 or hp * 5 <= max_hp. If max_hp = 15, then hp * 5 <= 15 means hp <= 3. So effectively hp <= 3.\n- At XL 5: max_hp = min(max_hitpoints, 75), divisor = 6. Returns True when hp <= 5 or hp * 6 <= 75, i.e., hp <= 12.\n- At XL 8: max_hp = min(max_hitpoints, 120), divisor = 7. Returns True when hp <= 5 or hp * 7 <= 120, i.e., hp <= 17.\n\nThe suggested threshold `hp < max/3 or hp < 8` would be:\n- At XL 1 with max_hp = 15: hp < 5 or hp < 8, i.e., hp <= 4 (since hp < 5 means hp <= 4). Wait, `hp < max/3` with max=15 means hp < 5, i.e., hp <= 4. And `hp < 8` means hp <= 7. So effectively hp <= 7 (since hp < 5 is more restrictive for very low HP, but hp < 8 allows up to 7).\n  \nActually, let me re-read the logic. The current code returns `hp <= 5 or hp * divisor <= max_hp`. With divisor=5 and max_hp=15, this is `hp <= 5 or hp * 5 <= 15` = `hp <= 5 or hp <= 3` = `hp <= 3`. So prayer triggers only at HP <= 3.\n\nThe suggested change to `hp < max/3 or hp < 8` with max_hp=15 would be `hp < 5 or hp < 8` = `hp <= 4 or hp <= 7` = `hp <= 7`. So prayer would trigger at HP <= 7, which is much more generous.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-express the suggested change. The comment says \"Raise the crisis threshold to match the potion threshold (HP < max/3 or HP < 8)\". The potion threshold at line 1831 is `hp < max_hp / 3 or hp < 8`. So the suggestion is to make `critically_low_hp` return the same condition.\n\nBut `critically_low_hp` doesn't have access to the exact max_hp in the same way. Let me think about how to modify it.\n\nActually, looking at the current code more carefully, `critically_low_hp` computes `max_hp = min(max_hp, 15 * level)` and then uses a divisor. The suggested change would simplify this to just check `hp < max_hp / 3 or hp < 8`, where max_hp is the actual max_hitpoints.\n\nLet me make the change. I'll modify `critically_low_hp` to use the simpler threshold.","time":{"start":1790518968525,"end":1790518995965}}}
