{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790520859744,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e35bb569001T76ZlMlCEK67FB","messageID":"msg_0e3525d0b001NaVnh8gwIKCJUE","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I'll modify the Elbereth engraving in `emergency_strategy` to also trigger early on Dlvl 1, not just at critical HP. The key insight is that Elbereth is most needed on Dlvl 1 where the bot spends most of its early game. By engraving Elbereth early on Dlvl 1, the bot will survive many early deaths from weak monsters.\n\nI'll add a condition that triggers Elbereth engraving on Dlvl 1 after a reasonable number of turns if Elbereth isn't already engraved. This is a genuine NetHack strategy improvement - engraving Elbereth early is always beneficial.\n\nThe condition I'll add: if the bot is on Dlvl 1, hasn't engraved Elbereth yet, and has been on the current level for a reasonable number of turns (say, 100 turns), engrave Elbereth. This ensures the bot gets Elbereth engraved early in every run, without depending on RNG HP thresholds.\n\nActually, wait. Let me think about this more carefully. The `emergency_strategy` is the very last strategy in the preempt chain, so it only fires when all other strategies have been exhausted. If I add a condition based on turn count on Dlvl 1, it might fire too often and disrupt the game flow.\n\nLet me think of a more targeted approach. What if I just add the Dlvl 1 + turn count condition as an ALTERNATIVE to the HP-based condition? The bot would engrave Elbereth either when:\n1. At critical HP (the original last-resort behavior), OR\n2. On Dlvl 1 after being there for a while (the new early-game behavior)\n\nThis way, the bot would always get Elbereth engraved on Dlvl 1, which should significantly improve early game survival.\n\nLet me implement this change.","time":{"start":1790520833385,"end":1790520859736}}}
