{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790521251566,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e361cab7001f6YpeKVOLsHqD6","messageID":"msg_0e361c7b400108UUs3E2Qid8eQ","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"This change is harmful! The early Dlvl 1 Elbereth engraving is making things much worse. The deltas are mostly negative, with seed 0 being the only one that improved (from 0.117 to 0.117, no change). Seeds 1 and 4 went from positive scores to starvation deaths at Dlvl 1.\n\nThe problem is that my condition `self.blstats.time > 200` is causing the bot to spend turns engraving Elbereth early, which delays other actions and leads to starvation or other deaths. The bot is engraving instead of managing food or fighting monsters.\n\nI need a different approach. Let me reconsider.\n\nThe issue is that engraving Elbereth takes time and actions, and if the bot engraves too early or too often, it can actually hurt the score by wasting turns that could be used for fighting, searching, or managing food.\n\nLet me go back to the drawing board. What focused change would reliably improve the score?\n\nLet me re-examine the problem. The bot scores 0.091 (mean across 15 seeds of hea-gno-neu-mal). The key issues are:\n1. Early deaths to weak monsters (many seeds die at Dlvl 1-3)\n2. Starvation (some seeds)\n3. Not getting deep enough (only seed 8 gets very deep)\n\nThe most impactful single change would be to ensure the bot survives the early game long enough to descend. Elbereth is the key tool for this, but my previous attempts at modifying the engraving threshold were either too RNG-sensitive or had negative side effects.\n\nLet me think about what change would be different this time...\n\nActually, let me look at this from a completely different angle. What if I modify the `proactive_sleep_strategy` to work when a sleep wand IS available, and the Healer just needs the gnome check removed? But Healers don't start with a sleep wand...\n\nWait, let me check: does the Healer ever find a sleep wand during the game? Maybe the proactive sleep strategy would help if the bot finds a sleep wand.\n\nActually, let me take yet another approach. Let me look at the `anger_peaceful_dwarf` strategy more carefully. For Healer-Gnome, this is skipped because the bot is a gnome. But what if I modify it to also provide some benefit for gnomes?\n\nNo, that doesn't make sense for gnomes who have the peaceful Mines route.\n\nLet me look at the `dig_down` strategy. This allows the bot to dig down when carrying a digging tool. For Healer-Gnome, the bot should find a pick-axe in the Mines and then use dig_down to descend quickly. Maybe improving the dig_down strategy would help.\n\nActually, let me re-read the global_strategy in global_logic.py to see how dig_down is used.\n\nLooking at lines 918-920:\n```python\n.preempt(self.agent, [\n    self.agent.dig_down(),\n])\n```\n\nThe `dig_down` strategy is at the very end of the preempt chain, so it only fires when all other strategies have been exhausted. Let me look at the `dig_down` method in agent.py.","time":{"start":1790521232055,"end":1790521251561}}}
