{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790521281263,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e3622c33001hoBKFEpGqVpoQj","messageID":"msg_0e36227cb0017oN5vPaR7xIjGD","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"Looking at the `dig_down` strategy, I see several important things:\n\n1. It only triggers when `experience_level >= 8` (line 1788-1790) - the deep phase has begun\n2. It only works on the main dungeon (not Mines) (line 1798)\n3. It requires a wand of digging OR a pick-axe (lines 1808-1813, 1822)\n4. The comment mentions \"Dig under a dust Elbereth\" - engraved before starting\n\nFor Healer-Gnome, the bot should find a pick-axe in the Mines (from peaceful dwarves) and then use dig_down to descend. But the current code only triggers at XP >= 8, and only on the main dungeon.\n\nWait, looking at line 1798: `if self.current_level().dungeon_number != Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM: yield False`. This means dig_down only works on the main dungeon (dungeon number 0). For Healer-Gnome, the bot goes to the Mines (dungeon number 2) after the Dlvl 1 grind. So dig_down wouldn't help in the Mines.\n\nBut the comment says \"Dig in the Mines too, down to Mines' End (Dlvl 10-13), instead of walking a found pick back up through hostile packs\". So maybe the code was intended to work in the Mines too, but the condition at line 1799 prevents it.\n\nActually, looking at lines 1798-1802:\n```python\nif self.current_level().dungeon_number != Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM:\n    yield False\n    return\nif self.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and self._mines_bottom_found:\n    yield False\n    return\n```\n\nThe first check prevents digging in the Mines entirely (except when _mines_bottom_found is True and we're in the Mines). The second check prevents digging when we've already found the Mines' End.\n\nSo dig_down is mainly for the main dungeon, not the Mines. For Healer-Gnome, the bot needs to get through the Mines first, then dig down the main dungeon.\n\nLet me think about what change would help Healer-Gnome specifically...\n\nActually, let me go back to basics. The per-seed analysis shows that the main problems are:\n1. Early deaths to weak monsters on Dlvl 1-3\n2. Starvation\n3. Not descending to deeper levels\n\nThe most focused and impactful change would be to ensure the bot survives the early game. Elbereth is the key, but my previous attempts had issues.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach. What if I modify the `proactive_sleep_strategy` to handle the case where the Healer doesn't have a sleep wand, by doing something else helpful? Or what if I modify it to only skip gnomes when no sleep wand is found, and run the strategy when a sleep wand IS available?\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-check: does the Healer ever find a sleep wand during the game? In NetHack, wands of sleep can be found in containers, on shelves, etc. The Healer might find one during the game. If the proactive_sleep_strategy helps even a few seeds, it could improve the mean.\n\nLet me test the proactive_sleep_strategy change (without the gnome check) on all 15 seeds to see if any seeds benefit.\n\nActually, I already tested this earlier and all deltas were 0.000 for 5 seeds. Let me test on 15 seeds to be sure.\n\nBut wait, I already removed the gnome check from the proactive_sleep_strategy earlier (in a previous edit). Let me check the current state of the code.\n\nActually, looking at my edits:\n1. I modified the Elbereth threshold (then reverted)\n2. I removed the gnome check from proactive_sleep_strategy\n3. I modified the prayer critically_low_hp\n4. I modified the Elbereth early-game engraving (which I just reverted)\n\nLet me check the current state of the proactive_sleep_strategy.","time":{"start":1790521257011,"end":1790521281257}}}
