{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790521854167,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e36afe49001703vFkT0eMF6ql","messageID":"msg_0e36afa1c001dGYYVbCUB2IlQX","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"The proactive_sleep_strategy change made things worse! The mean went from 0.0912 to 0.0853 (-0.0059). Some seeds improved (2, 8, 12, 13, 14) but many more worsened (1, 4, 8, 10, 11). Seed 8 went from 0.554 to 0.024 (-0.530) - a catastrophic failure for the best run.\n\nThe issue is that the proactive sleep strategy is disrupting the game RNG and causing more deaths than it prevents. The sleep wand is hard to find, and when it's used, it changes the game sequence in ways that don't generally improve survival.\n\nLet me revert this change and try something else.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The proactive_sleep_strategy uses the sleep wand proactively, but:\n1. Healers rarely find a sleep wand during the game\n2. When they do, using it proactively changes the RNG sequence\n3. The strategy can actually cause more harm than good\n\nSo the proactive_sleep_strategy is not the right change.\n\nLet me think about what other focused changes I could make...\n\nLooking at the codebase again, I've explored:\n1. Elbereth engraving threshold - mixed/negative results\n2. Proactive sleep for gnomes - negative results\n3. Prayer threshold - neutral results\n\nWhat about the `emergency_strategy` Elbereth engraving? Let me re-examine this. My earlier change added an early Dlvl 1 engraving condition, but it made things worse because the bot wasted turns engraving.\n\nWhat if I take a more moderate approach? Instead of adding the Dlvl 1 turn count condition, what if I just slightly modify the existing HP threshold? The current threshold is `hp < max/3 or hp < 8`. What if I change it to `hp < max/2.5 or hp < 10` or something similar?\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the original Elbereth change I made and then reverted. The original change was from `1/5 or < 5` to `1/2 or < 15`, which gave some impressive improvements for some seeds but worsened others. Then I changed to `1/3 or < 8` (which was the same as the existing code, since the original was `1/5 or < 5`). Then I reverted completely.\n\nLet me think about what single change would be most likely to improve the score consistently.\n\nActually, let me look at this from a different perspective. The task mentions `/refs/parent-eval.json` has per-seed results. But that file doesn't exist in the workspace. The task also mentions `attempts.md` with code under `attempts/`. These files are also missing.\n\nMaybe the /refs directory was supposed to be set up but isn't. Or maybe it's in a different location. Let me check if there's any way to access this data.\n\nActually, the task says: \"Start with /refs/CONTEXT.md — it lists what's there: a pristine copy of this bot (parent/), its per-seed results (parent-eval.json), and other changes that were tried with the score each reached (attempts.md, with their code under attempts/).\"\n\nBut these files don't exist. Maybe they were deleted or the git repo doesn't have them. Let me check git more carefully.","time":{"start":1790521835081,"end":1790521854161}}}
