{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790523794243,"sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","part":{"id":"prt_0e38861bf001pOFkRHzeSmt3Ri","messageID":"msg_0e3885db2001m1IXDIqLT3fn5d","sessionID":"ses_f1d0b999fffeBrMKM4fI8Jnoph","type":"reasoning","text":"The results are very mixed:\n- Seed 0: 0.117 → 0.426 (+0.309, huge improvement)\n- Seed 3: 0.037 → 0.507 (+0.470, huge improvement)\n- Seed 9: 0.037 → 0.126 (+0.089, improvement)\n- Seed 1: 0.075 → 0.037 (-0.038, slight worsening)\n- Seed 2: 0.024 → 0.000 (-0.024, worsening)\n- Seed 4: 0.117 → 0.000 (-0.117, worsening - starvation)\n- Seed 5: 0.021 → 0.000 (-0.021, worsening)\n- Seed 6: 0.029 → 0.000 (-0.029, worsening - starvation)\n- Seed 7: 0.126 → 0.000 (-0.126, worsening - sewer rat)\n- Seed 8: 0.554 → 0.000 (-0.554, catastrophic - best run destroyed)\n- Seed 9: 0.037 → 0.126 (+0.089, improvement)\n\nNew mean: 0.1095 vs old mean (these 10 seeds): 0.1137\n\nSo the mean slightly decreased from 0.1137 to 0.1095. And seed 8 (the best run at 0.554) was destroyed again.\n\nThe pattern is clear: the Elbereth threshold change helps some seeds (0, 3, 9) but destroys others (1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8). Seed 8 is consistently the casualty.\n\nThe problem is that the Elbereth engraving is RNG-sensitive. Engraving Elbereth early changes the game RNG sequence, which benefits some seeds (where it prevents early deaths) but destroys others (where it causes the bot to waste turns or change the game flow in a detrimental way).\n\nI need a different approach. Let me think about what change would be less RNG-sensitive...\n\nActually, let me reconsider the entire approach. The task says \"Make ONE focused change that raises its score.\" The current score is 0.091. I need to raise it.\n\nLooking at all the changes I've tried:\n1. Elbereth threshold changes - mixed, some seeds benefit greatly but seed 8 always suffers\n2. Proactive sleep - negative overall\n3. Prayer threshold - neutral\n4. Early Dlvl 1 Elbereth - negative\n5. Healer in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY - negative\n\nWhat change have I NOT tried that might work?\n\nLet me look at the codebase one more time for other opportunities...\n\nActually, let me look at the `follow_guard` strategy. This handles the Quest guard, but Healer-Gnome starts in the main dungeon. Not relevant.\n\nLet me look at the `read_magic_mapping` strategy. This reads magic mapping scrolls. Not sure if this would help.\n\nLet me look at the `dip_for_excalibur` strategy. Only for lawful characters. Healer-Neutral, so not relevant.\n\nLet me look at the `offer_corpses` strategy. Sacrificing corpses on altars for artifact. Could be relevant for Healer, but the effect would be small.\n\nActually, let me look at the `global_strategy` preemption order one more time. The strategies are preempted in this order:\n1. current_strategy().repeat() - main milestone progression\n2. solve_sokoban_strategy\n3. offer_corpses\n4. wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy\n5. cure_disease\n6. eat_corpses_from_ground\n7. follow_guard\n8. anger_peaceful_dwarf\n9. fight2\n10. engulfed_fight\n11. proactive_sleep_strategy\n12. emergency_strategy\n13. read_magic_mapping\n14. dig_down\n\nWhat if I change the preemption order? For example, what if I move `fight2` before `anger_peaceful_dwarf`, or what if I move `emergency_strategy` earlier?\n\nActually, the preemption order determines which strategy gets to act first when multiple strategies are applicable. Changing the order could change the game sequence, but it's not clear would improve the score consistently.\n\nLet me try one more thing: what if I modify the `current_strategy` to ensure the bot leaves the Dlvl 1 grind at the right time? The current condition for Healer is `experience_level >= _grind_xl()` which defaults to 8. What if I lower this to 5 or 6?\n\nActually, looking at the `ROLE_GRIND_XL` dict:\n```python\nROLE_GRIND_XL = {}\n```\n\nIt's empty, so `_grind_xl()` returns `GRIND_XL = 8` for all roles including Healer. What if I set `ROLE_GRIND_XL[Character.HEALER] = 5`? This would cause the Healer to leave the Dlvl 1 grind at XP 5 instead of XP 8, which would let the bot descend sooner.\n\nBut the comment says \"Healers do better finishing the grind.\" So lowering the grind XL might cause Healers to descend too early and die from lack of XP.\n\nLet me test this change anyway. Maybe the original assessment was wrong, or maybe the current game balance is different.\n\nActually, let me just try it and see what happens.","time":{"start":1790523761087,"end":1790523794233}}}
